# Product isolation at integration boundaries

Shared instrumentation lives in `ddtrace/contrib/internal/`. Do not import AI Guard,
IAST, or AppSec implementation code into contrib patches or require those products to be enabled.
Use `ddtrace.internal.core` events so optional products register their own listeners.

- Reuse an existing event where possible; otherwise define the producer payload in contrib.
- Preserve `allow_raise=True` where listener `Exception` subclasses must reach the caller.
  `BaseException` subclasses propagate regardless; see `ddtrace/internal/core/event_hub.py`.
- Register listeners inside the product's enabled lifecycle, and convert provider objects there.
- Check import direction with `dependency-direction-analysis` when crossing package boundaries,
  and check cycles with `circular-import-analysis` when adding or moving modules.

References: `ddtrace/aiguard/_listener.py` and `ddtrace/contrib/internal/openai/patch.py`.
`scripts/import-analysis/layers.json` owns the zone definitions and intentional exceptions;
contrib-to-tracing is allowed, so do not generalize the security-product rule to every import.
